"SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-8064557-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8064557</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9091388-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9091388</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="WO-1996031921-A1" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>WO</country><doc-number>1996031921</doc-number><kind>A1</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1093169A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SATO EIICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEIKO EPSON CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, EIICHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEIKO EPSON CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SATO EIICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, EIICHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method of manufacturing a semiconductor device which causes no short circuit therein because of dust floating in the air, a semiconductor device, a narrow pitch connector, a micromachine such as an electrostatic actuator or a piezoelectric actuator, and an ink jet head, an ink jet printer, a liquid crystal panel, and an electronic apparatus including these devices are disclosed. The method of manufacturing a plurality of semiconductor devices (20) by dicing a silicon wafer (30) comprises making grooves (30a) covered with insulating layers in the silicon wafer and extending across dicing lines and dicing the wafer along the dicing lines.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne un procédé de fabrication de semi-conducteur qui permet d'éviter un phénomène de court-circuit dans ledit dispositif par suite de la poussière en suspension dans l'air, un dispositif semi-conducteur, un connecteur à écartement étroit, une micromachine telle qu'un actionneur électrostatique ou piézo-électrique, une tête d'impression à jet d'encre, une imprimante à jet d'encre, un panneau d'affichage à cristaux liquides et un dispositif électronique comprenant les organes précités. Le procédé utilisé pour la fabrication d'une pluralité de dispositifs semi-conducteurs (20) consiste à découper en dés une tranche de silicium (30), à pratiquer des rainures (30a) recouvertes de couches isolantes dans la tranche de silicium, à les continuer au travers des lignes de découpage et à scier la tranche le long de ces dernières lignes.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>